  `claude mcp list` / `obs doctor --layer mcp`). Removed mcp_config.json (unreferenced,
  hardcoded another user's home dir). Also fixed a stale `obs version # should print
  3.3.0` in the claude-mcp tutorial (PR #108). mkdocs build --strict clean both times;
  live site verified post-deploy (fetched claude-integration/ page, confirmed
  configure_mcp.py instructions + v4.4.2 sidebar badge). Caught mid-fix: `git add
  file1 file2 ... badpath` silently aborts staging ALL listed paths when one doesn't
  match a file on disk — a `git rm`'d path in the same `git add` call dropped 4 real
  edits with no error; recovered by checking `git show --stat HEAD` and re-staging.
  v4.4.2 RELEASED 2026-09-16: release PR #106 (dev→main, regular merge aeb2c55), main CI
  green (CI + Deploy Docs), tag v4.4.2 + GitHub release published
  (https://github.com/Data-Wise/obsidian-cli-ops/releases/tag/v4.4.2), Homebrew tap
  auto-synced (data-wise/homebrew-tap PR #226, auto-merged). dev/main back in sync.
  data-wise/homebrew-tap PR #225 merged 2026-09-16 (squash 698e195, tap `main`):
  migrated `post_install` (deprecated) to `post_install_steps` on the obsidian-cli-ops
  formula. The DSL's `run` block is evaluated at formula-definition (class-body) time,
  before any Formula instance exists — a live accessor call like `libexec` inside it
  fails `brew style`'s FormulaAudit/InstallSteps cop. Fixed via Homebrew's `{{libexec}}`
  run-time template token (expanded later against the real instance), confirmed correct
  by reading Homebrew's own `install_steps.rb` and reconfirmed via a real
  `brew reinstall --build-from-source` showing correctly-resolved paths. Also: bundled
  `scripts/configure_mcp.py` into the formula (`libexec/scripts/`, was missing entirely)
  so the caveats' MCP registration command actually resolves; `revision 1` bumped;
  caveats' MCP section rewritten to real `claude mcp add`/`claude mcp list` commands
  (not the retired claude_desktop_config.json flow, not a nonexistent marketplace-plugin
  slug — obsidian-cli-ops has no marketplace.json entry). CI gotcha hit + fixed: the tap's
  push-triggered "Regen vs committed" check diffs HEAD against the *previous commit on
  the branch*, not against main — a 3rd review-only commit (test assertion + comment, no
  content requiring its own revision bump) spuriously failed that check even though the
  pull_request-triggered run of the same check (correctly diffed against main) passed.
  Fixed by squashing the branch's 3 commits into 1 (git reset --soft origin/main +
  recommit + force-push) before merging — eliminates the false-positive for any
  single-commit PR. (See wiki finding on homebrew-tap's check-revision-bump.sh.)
  configure_mcp.py Cellar-path bug fixed + merged 2026-09-16 (PR #105, squash b81c47a,
  dev): `repo_dir = Path(__file__).resolve()`
  plus three more `.resolve()` calls on the derived server-script path dereferenced
  Homebrew's `opt/` stable symlink down to the version-pinned Cellar path whenever the
  script ran via the tap's own caveats-suggested invocation
  (`python3 $(brew --prefix obsidian-cli-ops)/libexec/scripts/configure_mcp.py`) —
  baking a path `brew upgrade` deletes into the registered `claude mcp add` args. Same
  fragility class as the v4.4.0 venv_python `.resolve()` fix, this time for the server
  script rather than the interpreter; `_resolve_python()`'s interpreter path was
  unaffected (it re-derives via `brew --prefix` independently). Dropped all 4
  `.resolve()` calls on the `__file__`-derived path. New regression test
  `src/python/tests/test_configure_mcp_symlink.py` (subprocess-level, opt/-symlink
  layout, no `claude` on PATH so no live-registry side effects) — confirmed it FAILS
  against the pre-fix code (planted-defect check) and PASSES against the fix. Full
  suite re-run in an ephemeral `uv run --python 3.12` env (no local dev venv with
  pytest+py>=3.10 was available): 637 passed / 142 skipped, no regressions. CI green
  (Clean-install smoke test, test, validate). Shipped in v4.4.2 (see above).
