  MCP registration mechanism fixed + merged 2026-09-16 (PR #103, squash fe81e6f, dev): CONFIRMED
  claude_desktop_config.json is repurposed for Cowork/epitaxy UI prefs on the unified Claude Code +
  Cowork desktop app (2.110.0) and carries no mcpServers key at all — real MCP registration goes
  through the claude CLI → ~/.claude.json (user scope)/.mcp.json (project scope). configure_mcp.py
  now calls `claude mcp add -s user` instead of hand-editing that file, and its interpreter
  resolution gained the missing Homebrew-venv tier (mirrors obs.zsh's _obs_resolve_python) — the old
  code fell straight to ambient python3 on a Homebrew-only install, which lacks the mcp package.
  obs doctor's mcp-config/mcp-entry checks renamed _CLAUDE_DESKTOP_CONFIG_PATHS → _MCP_CONFIG_PATHS
  to match; same DoctorResult ids/shape, updated tests (unit + dogfood + e2e). Full suite 636
  passed/4 skipped unchanged, e2e/test_e2e_doctor_mcp.py 4/4 passed. Live-verified on this machine:
  `claude mcp list` shows obsidian-ops ✔ Connected; running the fix directly showed 7/7 mcp-layer
  checks pass. CI green (test/validate/Clean-install smoke test), no leaks in diff. (See memory
  mcp-config-app-owned-not-static.)
