  dev-only fixes, uncommitted-to-committed (2026-09-15, prior to this release cut):
  (1) Python floor raised 3.9→3.10 (e1f5c6d) — pyproject.toml's `requires-python = ">=3.9"` was
  unresolvable: `mcp>=1.27.2` is a core (non-optional) dependency requiring Python >=3.10, so pip/uv
  dependency resolution failed outright on 3.9 (confirmed via uv's resolver); CI never actually
  tested 3.9 (matrix is 3.11/3.12 only). Bumped requires-python/classifiers/black+mypy targets and
  10 doc/status files asserting "Python 3.9+". doctor.py's runtime check was left alone — it already
  treated 3.9 as warn-tier, not a claimed floor.
  (2) board.py config-read reconciliation (083d78d) — BoardEngine._configured_board_path() (added
  uncommitted, this session, for the board.path config override / Issue #86 follow-up) was
  duplicating config_loader.py's YAML-parse/error-handling. Extracted config_loader.read_unified_doc()
  (existence+PyYAML-guard+safe_load, no vault.root requirement) and had both _load_unified() and
  board.py call it — deliberately NOT via config_loader.load()/ObsConfig, since load() requires
  vault.root and would silently drop a board-only config.
  (3) SPEC + GRILL + implementation: vault.root made Optional (42918b9 spec, a659e8f grill — 5
  branches resolved — 6eb7619 implementation) so a vault-less (e.g. board.path-only) config.yaml is
  visible to `obs config show` instead of reporting "no config found". `obs config validate` needed
  ZERO code changes — its existing `if not cfg.root` check already enforces "vault-less still
  fails validate" once root can be None. templates_resolved raises ValueError (not silent None);
  _to_yaml() guards against writing literal `root: "None"`. 8 new tests; full suite 629→636 passed,
  4 skipped throughout, zero regressions.
